      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "67213e0157887a5d00d69a6d",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The biggest issue I see with this feature, would be UI/UX when placing the portal. If you aren't allowed to place the portal in one of these zones, how would it be communicated to the user?\n\nCurrently if you try to place it in a spawn area, it just tells you you can't place it there. But if these zones are suddenly very big, it might confuse players a lot more.\n\nEither the world creator should be able to attach a small text, explaining to the user where they can place the portal. Such as: \"Portals can only be place in the lobby area.\" The main issue would that would be localization, since we can't expect a world creator to know all the supported languages.\n\nOr the world creator could define coordinates (or a reference object) that an arrow will then point the user towards as a simply way of saying \"you can place the portal in this direction.\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
